% Each use written in a rule gets its own expansion budget: after the
% first use fails with MacroExpansionTooDeep, the second still expands.
% Its expansion then reports its own error, which shows it was reached.
:- module(macro_budget_reset).
:- chr_constraint r/1.
:- macro grow(X) ---> [grow(s(X))].
:- macro second(X) ---> [missing(X)].
r(X) <=> grow(X), second(X).
